Need to work on this a lot but include
For modifying the location of the spoiler, one can go to the Accelerate Wind Onshape in the Ike > Vesta folder. Use the Vesta_Simple file along with the Vesta Spoiler file to create the assembly that you want. To export the spoiler in the correct location, a litle finagling is required, where you need to export the Vesta_Simple and Spoiler files as one part (on Fine resolution). Then, in WSL, run the surfaceCheck function on the file. It will decompose the file into 2 parts, a spoiler part and a building part. You can get rid of the building part as it is formed in the blockMesh, but save the spoiler part as spoiler.obj and include it in your constant/triSurface folder. This will mean the spoiler is in the correct location and orientation in the actual simulation. There might be an easier way to do this, but always verify that the spoiler was exported in the correct spot.
